$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-forgot-password
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">

<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-forgot-password-page" id="fp-top">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/login">Log in</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Password reminder</span>
  </nav>

  <!-- mgdb-hero-basic, not mgdb-hero: the full hero is a two-column grid whose
       first column is the emblem, so a hero body with no emblem beside it lands
       in a 150px-to-17% column and the title sets one letter per line. This is
       the same hero /login uses, which also keeps the two account pages
       looking like a pair. -->
  <section class="mgdb-hero-basic" aria-labelledby="fp-title">
    <span class="mgdb-hero-basic-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 84 84" role="presentation" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="30" cy="42" r="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="5"/>
        <path d="M43 42h23" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M58 42v10M66 42v7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <circle cx="30" cy="42" r="4" fill="#2f5e2a"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <div>
      <h1 id="fp-title">Password reminder</h1>
      <p>Curator accounts store a <strong>hint</strong> you chose when the account was made, not a recoverable password. Give the username or the e-mail address on the account and the hint is sent to that address.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="fp-form-section" aria-labelledby="fp-form-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="fp-form-title">Find your account</h2></div>
    </div>

    @(form
    <form class="fp-form" method="post" action="/forgot_password">
      <div class="mgdb-field fp-field">
        <label class="mgdb-label" for="fp-term">Username or e-mail address</label>
        <input class="mgdb-input" type="text" id="fp-term" name="term" maxlength="100"
               autocomplete="username" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" required
               aria-describedby="fp-hint" />
        <p class="mgdb-hint" id="fp-hint">Whichever you remember. The hint only ever goes to the address already on the account.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mgdb-form-actions">
        <button class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" type="submit">Send my hint</button>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/login">Back to log in</a>
      </div>
    </form>
    )

    @(sent {display: off}
    <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info fp-sent" role="status">
      <div>
        <strong>If that matches an account, the hint is on its way.</strong>
        <p>It is sent to the e-mail address already on the account, so check that inbox &mdash; and its spam folder. Nothing is sent if no account matches, and this page will not tell you which happened.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-form-actions fp-sent-actions">
      <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/login">Go to log in</a>
      <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/forgot_password">Try another address</a>
    </div>
    )
  </section>

  <section id="fp-help" aria-labelledby="fp-help-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="fp-help-title">If that does not help</h2></div>
    </div>

    <ul class="fp-help-list">
      <li>
        <strong>The hint does not remind you</strong>
        <span>Write to the MaizeGDB team through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and we can reset the account.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You are not sure the account exists</strong>
        <span>Curator accounts are for community annotation. Browsing, searching and downloading all work without one.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You want a new account</strong>
        <span>MaizeGDB is not issuing new annotation accounts at this time. To ask about curator access, use the <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a>.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
)
